  "level": 1,
  "question": {
    "text": "If in a parallelogram $\\mathrm{ABDC}$, the coordinates of $\\mathrm{A}, \\mathrm{B}$ and $\\mathrm{C}$ are respectively (1,2),(3,4) and $(2,5),$ then the equation of the diagonal $\\mathrm{AD}$ is :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "mSj7j",
      "text": "$5 x-3 y+1=0$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "2FGsl",
      "text": "$5 x+3 y-11=0$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "KYix4",
      "text": "$3 x-5 y+7=0$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "wPzTy",
      "text": "$3 x+5 y-13=0$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Since, in parallelogram mid points of both diagonals\r\n\r\ncoinsides.\r\n\r\n$\\therefore$ mid-point of $A D=$ mid-point of $B C$\r\n\r\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/BKKZMNN-dDGVSh9X7xx5JWtAgaS6zr89_tOa2GMnnjM.original.fullsize.png\"><br>\r\n\r\n$\\left(\\frac{x_{1}+1}{2}, \\frac{y_{1}+2}{2}\\right)=\\left(\\frac{3+2}{2}, \\frac{4+5}{2}\\right)$\r\n\r\n$\\therefore \\quad\\left(x_{1}, y_{1}\\right)=(4,7)$\r\n\r\nThen, equation of $A D$ is,\r\n\r\n$y-7=\\frac{2-7}{1-4}(x-4)$\r\n\r\n$y-7=\\frac{5}{3}(x-4)$\r\n\r\n$3 y-21=5 x-20$\r\n\r\n$5 x-3 y+1=0$",
    "image": null
  },
